session:pr152Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Enables oxttl's rdf-12 cargo feature in turtle/Cargo.toml and extends intern_term in turtle/src/lib.rs to handle Term::Triple, interning RDF 1.2 triple terms (<<( s p o )>>) via Datastore::add_triple_term. This covers Turtle, TriG, N-Triples, and N-Quads since all four parsers share oxttl's term model. Un-ignores test_triple_term_as_object in turtle/tests/rdf12.rs (object-position triple terms) — passes. Un-ignores the 8 W3C RDF 1.2 positive/negative syntax conformance tests (Turtle, N-Triples, N-Quads, TriG) in tests/w3c_rdf12_conformance.rs — all pass. Empirically confirms and documents the \"subject-position blocker\" from docs/plans/RDF12_PLAN.md: oxttl 0.2.3 (even with rdf-12 enabled) rejects <<( in subject position outright with TurtleSyntaxError { message: \"<<( is not a valid subject or graph name\" }, matching oxrdf 0.3.3's Triple::subject: NamedOrBlankNode, which has no variant for a nested triple term. This is a genuine grammar-level limitation in the current pinned library versions (confirmed latest available), not something work-around-able at the application layer. What stays ignored (and why) 4 subject-position tests in turtle/tests/rdf12.rs (test_triple_term_as_subject, test_same_triple_term_in_two_named_graphs, test_nested_triple_term, test_triple_term_with_literal_object) — each carries a comment pointing to the empirical finding above." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:152 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr152 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
